Source: linux-entra-bridge
Section: web
Priority: optional
Maintainer: Patrick Haar <Pihaar@users.noreply.github.com>
Build-Depends: debhelper-compat (= 13)
Standards-Version: 4.6.2
Homepage: https://github.com/Pihaar/linux-entra-bridge
Rules-Requires-Root: no

Package: linux-entra-bridge
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, python3 (>= 3.6), python3-dbus
Description: Microsoft Entra ID SSO bridge for Linux browsers
 Enables Microsoft Entra ID single sign-on in Firefox, Chromium, and related
 browsers on Linux by bridging to the microsoft-identity-broker D-Bus service.
 A native messaging host obtains the PRT SSO cookie from the broker and the
 browser extension sets it, so the browser can satisfy Conditional Access
 policies that otherwise only work in Microsoft Edge.
